                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Honestly I had a tough time writing a review for Elsewhere High Chapter 1.\n\nIt's just painfully average. Unfortunately steam doesn't have neutral rating so I will give it a positive one BUT ONLY because its free, small in download size, and it works.\n\nFrom a technical perspective it's not good. The interface doesn't look good and it's missing some basic VN options (e.g. text speed), art style is also nothing special (It's passable). It does have sound affects/music's which are pretty good except you can't turn them off or lower them (there is literally no sound option !?!). Also steam overlay doesn't work.\n\nThe story wise it's ok and personally I enjoyed it. Writing and pacing is better then your average steam visual novel and I haven't noticed any grammar mistakes. You do get a few choices through the story (two at the time) but the problem is choices are pretty much useless considering they don't affect the ending.\n\nAlso if you want 100% achievement completion you'll have to buy chapter 2. \n\nOverall 5/10. You should give it a try but unfortunately don't expect too much.\n\nI do think that this developer can make a better VN in the future if they polish technical aspects of it and some other minor things.",
